{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"schema\"","\"framework\"","\"framework_sha256\"","\"framework_bytes\"","\"research_cutoff\"","\"market_date\"","\"company\"","\"symbol\"","\"isin\"","\"venue\"","\"scope\"","\"scores\"","\"market\"","\"financial_metrics\"","\"model_rows\"","\"reverse_roots\"","\"capacity_rows\"","\"path_count\"","\"all_paths_file\"","\"all_paths_sha256\"","\"path_index_file\"","\"report_file\"","\"input_hashes\"","\"generated_hashes\"","\"small-micro-cap-v3-rapid-fleet-1\"","\"Small/Micro-Cap Stock Research Master Prompt v3.0\"","\"68d4de4255427df276318d0231530b867a453e740c74150e9768bf1387224137\"","72939","\"2026-10-20\"","\"2026-10-19\"","\"Rapid Fleet Management Services Limited\"","\"RAPIDFLEET\"","\"INE0QX901013\"","\"NSE Emerge\"","\"Standalone AS accounts, INR crore unless specified; source-safe authored extracts; no investment order or personalized advice\"","\"factors\"","\"gates\"","\"BQS\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"caps\"","\"classification\"","\"rounding\"","\"sensitivity\"","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"DUR\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"BAL\"","\"EXEC\"","\"EARN\"","\"R\"","\"D\"","\"P\"","\"L\"","\"score\"","\"confidence\"","\"evidence\"","\"basis\"","\"contrary\"","3","\"Medium\"","\"E02\"","\"E03\"","\"E12\"","\"E13\"","\"Recurring control and authorization failures: FY24 no commensurate internal audit, FY24–25 incomplete audit trail, FY25 employee misappropriation, FY26 material RPT approval and MD pay-limit breaches, plus mislabelled RPT comparatives. No promoter diversion alleged.\"","\"Financial and IFC opinions are unmodified. Promoter dividend waiver and subsequent prospective RPT approvals are positives, but do not erase historical lapses.\"","4","\"E04\"","\"E05\"","\"Bidding-based road transport and hired capacity are replicable. High historical customer concentration limits bargaining power.\"","\"Specialized ODC execution and customer relationships are useful, but excess returns and switching costs are unverified.\"","null","\"Low\"","\"E06\"","\"The preselected five-year organic window and three-year fallback cannot be isolated from fuel pass-through and owned/hired mix. Nominal reported CAGRs remain diagnostics; underlying REV is NS.\"","\"Reported sales and value added expanded materially. No acquisition was identified, but a clean demand bridge is missing.\"","6","\"E11\"","\"Existing auto, renewable and project-cargo customers provide accessible demand. The fleet investment and short-tenor orders demonstrate real commercial activity.\"","\"Order cancellations, remaining backlog and current customer concentration are ND; capex alone does not prove future volumes.\"","\"E10\"","\"E07\"","\"The recent three-year incremental return proxy is below the analytical13–17% cost-of-capital range. Fleet and receivable investment absorbed substantial capital.\"","\"The five-year proxy is stronger and new fleet cohorts are immature; aggregate returns are not project IRRs.\"","\"High\"","\"E08\"","\"Recent three-year CFO/PAT is weak; aged and unbilled receivables increased. FY25 printed CFO retains investment gains.\"","\"FY22–23 conversion was stronger and FY26 CFO was positive, although supplier credit materially supported FY22.\"","\"E09\"","\"E14\"","\"October cash/debt and the amount and terms of Q1 bank finance are unknown. Linked scenarios cannot establish actual funding resilience, so BAL is NS.\"","\"March leverage was modest, cash equivalents existed, and audits report no loan default. Gate3 is not automatically Fail.\"","5","\"Reported trip activity, fleet additions and complex ODC delivery demonstrate operating execution. No formal earnings target is invented.\"","\"Fleet rollforward, customer cohorts and collection outcomes remain unreconciled; operational progress is not cash-conversion excellence.\"","\"E01\"","\"FY26 operating profit and normalized current-share earnings improved. FY25 investment gains and IPO weighted-share EPS complicate comparisons.\"","\"Operating EBITDA increased and the other-income contribution fell; earnings growth is not solely non-operating.\"","\"No defensible unconditional five-year IRR exists while entry funding is unknown. Conditional rescue outcomes are not substituted into R.\"","\"The model retains feasible and failed conditional returns and explicit12/15/18% hurdles.\"","\"Customer concentration, unbilled/aged receivables and upfront hire funding expose permanent capital loss. A rescued bear case may still dilute and lose value.\"","\"Tangible fleet and March liquidity provide some protection; actual insolvency is not established.\"","\"Audited FY26 P/E is about12.4x and does not plainly require exceptional growth. Removing other income raises the earnings multiple.\"","\"March cash is not current excess cash; an inexpensive headline multiple cannot resolve funding or governance risk.\"","\"E15\"","\"The prescribed7.504-session reference exit starts atL5. A disclosed one-point implementation haircut reflects15 absent issuer rows and600-share lot granularity.\"","\"All latest20 sessions contain trades and median turnover is similar; the stock is not labelled untradeable.\"","\"G1\"","\"G2\"","\"G3\"","\"G4\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"Conditional\"","\"Repeated control and authorization failures, but promoter diversion is not established. GOV3 activates the score cap independently.\"","\"Hold\"","\"RPT comparative errors, cash-flow vintages and unverified entry funding prevent a fully reliable investment conclusion.\"","\"Conditional model breaches are not proof of actual default. Disclosed Q1 bank funding lacks amount and terms.\"","\"The600-share lot and7.504-session reference exit constrain implementation; spread and current restrictions are ND.\"","\"weights\"","\"contributions\"","\"known_sum\"","\"coverage\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"raw\"","\"raw_display\"","\"raw_bounds\"","\"cap\"","\"post_cap_bounds\"","\"final\"","\"final_display\"","\".20\"","\".12\"","\".10\"","\".08\"","\"0.60\"","\"0.80\"","\"0.48\"","\"0.30\"","\"0.40\"","\"3.18\"","\"0.20\"","\"NS\"","\"3.38\"","\"5.18\"","\"3\"","\".40\"","\".15\"","\"1.20\"","\"0.75\"","\"2.85\"","\"3.25\"","\"6.85\"","\"5\"","\"unpropagated_bounds\"","\"nested_bound_method\"","\".25\"","\".35\"","\"0.50\"","\"1.70\"","\"2.80\"","\"5.95\"","\"2.30\"","\"7.70\"","\"NS BQS remains NS; propagate its post-cap numerical bounds, not unconstrained1–10.\"","\"GOV3 caps BQS and IAS at3. CASH3 persistent poor realization caps GQS at5. Missing inputs keep all affected composites NS even where capped bounds collapse. Gate1 remains Conditional, not an allegation of fraud.\"","\"Avoid — governance; separately Hold — unresolved data; excluded from investable rankings\"","\"Decimal precision32;ROUND_HALF_UP one-decimal display;no renormalization;NS != zero; mathematical bounds not estimates\"","\"factor\"","\"change\"","-1","\"2.98\"","\"4.98\"","1","\"3.58\"","\"5.38\"","\"2.9450\"","\"6.5450\"","\"0.36\"","\"3.06\"","\"3.26\"","\"5.06\"","\"0.45\"","\"2.70\"","\"3.10\"","\"6.70\"","\"3.30\"","\"3.50\"","\"5.30\"","\"3.00\"","\"3.40\"","\"7.00\"","\"price\"","\"date\"","\"shares\"","\"lot\"","\"market_cap\"","\"60_sessions\"","\"present_sessions\"","\"absent_sessions\"","\"mean_60\"","\"median_60\"","\"mean_20\"","\"median_20\"","\"reference_position\"","\"conservative_daily_value\"","\"exit_days\"","\"one_lot_cost\"","\"three_lot_position\"","\"four_lot_position\"","\"PE_reported\"","\"PE_normalized\"","\"PB\"","\"EV_March_anchor\"","\"EV_EBITDA_March_anchor\"","\"net_debt_EBITDA_March_anchor\"","\"date_warning\"","\"spread\"","\"ASM_GSM\"","\"static_master_PricRg\"","\"L_start\"","\"L_haircut\"","\"L_final\"","\"208.50\"","7434800","600","\"155.01558\"","60","45","15","\"1904736.00\"","\"1332600.00\"","\"1444728.00\"","\"1336665.00\"","\"500000\"","\".02\"","\".05\"","\"18.760318174996247936365000750413\"","\"7.5041272699984991745460003001651\"","\"3.7520636349992495872730001500825\"","\"125100.00\"","\"375300.